{"path":"experimental/scope_exit/release","title":"std::experimental::scope_exit<EF>::release","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::scope_exit&lt;EF&gt;::</span>release","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/scope_exit/release","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"Makes the scope_exit inactive.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-libfund_ts_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> release<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-libfund-ts-3 t-mark-ts\">(library fundamentals TS v3)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Makes the <code>scope_exit</code> inactive.\n</p><p>Once a <code>scope_exit</code> is inactive, it cannot become active again, and will not call its exit function on destruction.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p><code>release</code> may be either manually called or automatically called by <code>scope_exit</code>'s move constructor.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div t-dsc-member-nobold-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/scope_exit/scope_exit\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>(constructor)</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  constructs a new <code>scope_exit</code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div t-dsc-member-nobold-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/scope_exit/~scope_exit\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>(destructor)</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  calls the exit function when the scope is exited if the <code>scope_exit</code> is active, then destroys the <code>scope_exit</code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/scope_exit","title":"std::experimental::scope_exit"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::scope_exit<EF>::release","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Makes the scope_exit inactive."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Notes","note":"release may be either manually called or automatically called by scope_exit's move constructor."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"(constructor)","note":"constructs a new scope_exit"},{"label":"(destructor)","note":"calls the exit function when the scope is exited if the scope_exit is active, then destroys the scope_exit"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":88,"codeBlockCount":0}
